    "answer": {
      "short": "$30\\text{ m}$",
      "worked": "Let $h$ be the tree height and $d$ Bob's horizontal distance from its base, both in metres. Using tangent in each right triangle,\n$$\\begin{align*}h&=10\\tan60^\\circ\\\\h&=10\\sqrt3\\\\d&=\\frac{h}{\\tan30^\\circ}\\\\d&=\\frac{10\\sqrt3}{1/\\sqrt3}\\\\d&=30.\\end{align*}$$\nBob is exactly $30\\text{ m}$ from the base of the tree.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
